                "senderName": "NWS Riverton WY",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 29 at 1:07PM MDT until August 30 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Riverton WY",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, northwest, and west central Wyoming,\nincluding the following areas, in central Wyoming, Wind River\nMountains West. In northwest Wyoming, Absaroka Mountains, Jackson\nHole, Teton and Gros Ventre Mountains and Yellowstone National\nPark. In west central Wyoming, Salt River and Wyoming Ranges and\nStar Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Increased moisture from the Pacific will move across northwest\nWyoming through the weekend, bringing an extended chance for\nshowers and thunderstorms. The increased moisture will have the\npotential to produce locally heavy rainfall, providing excessive\nrunoff in flood-prone and low-lying areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
